.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg 1  "ifg 0.9.0"
.SH NAME
ifg \- Work with IronForge repositories, issues, pull requests, CI and releases from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg\fR [\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-template\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work with IronForge repositories, issues, pull requests, CI and releases from the terminal.
.PP
`ifg` talks to the IronForge REST API with a personal access token. The token is validated by `auth login`, stored in `hosts.toml` (in `IRONFORGE_CONFIG_DIR`, else `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ironforge`, else the platform default), and reused by every command. `token_store = "keyring"` moves it to the system keychain, but never while `IRONFORGE_CONFIG_DIR` is set. With both `IRONFORGE_URL` and `IRONFORGE_PAT` set, the stored config is not read at all.
.PP
Machine\-readable output: `\-\-json` prints the server\*(Aqs own field names, `\-q/\-\-template` renders a small template per result (`{{.number}} {{.title}}`, `{{range .labels}}{{.}} {{end}}`). Colors, relative timestamps and the pager only switch on when stdout is a terminal.
.PP
Long\-tail API surface (wiki, webhooks, packages, secrets, …) is reachable through `ifg api <path>`.
.PP
Scripts and AI agents should pass `\-\-no\-input` (or set `IFG_NO_INPUT=1`). Anything that would ask a person a question then fails at once with exit code 2 and names the flag to pass instead. `\-\-no\-input` is not `\-\-yes`: a destructive command still needs `\-\-yes` to run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fI<NAME|URL>\fR
Host name from the config, or a base URL like https://forge.example.com

Resolution order: this flag, `IRONFORGE_URL`, the repository\*(Aqs git remote (when run inside a checkout), then `default_host` from the config file. A NAME needs the stored config, so with both `IRONFORGE_URL` and `IRONFORGE_PAT` set, pass a URL instead.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<OWNER/NAME>\fR
Target repository as OWNER/NAME, or a full remote URL

Inside a git checkout `ifg` infers OWNER/NAME from `origin`, so the flag is only needed outside a repository or to target another one.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output JSON (server field names) instead of a table

Field names are the server\*(Aqs own, so `jq` expressions from the API docs work unchanged. Mutually exclusive with `\-\-template`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
Render each result through a small template (`{{.number}} {{.title}}`, nested paths allowed; lists render once per row)

Supported subset: `{{.field}}`, `{{.nested.field}}`, `{{.array.0}}`, `{{range .list}}…{{end}}` (nestable; objects iterate their values) and the escapes `\\n` / `\\t`. Missing fields render empty. Lists render the template once per item, so `{{range}}` is only needed for nested arrays such as an issue\*(Aqs labels.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colored output (also honors NO_COLOR)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt: fail with exit code 2 where a person would be asked

Use in scripts and by AI agents. A confirmation then refuses and names `\-\-yes`, `auth login` needs `\-\-with\-token`, `\-\-editor` is refused (use `\-t`/`\-b`), the pager is skipped and git subprocesses do not prompt. This is NOT `\-\-yes`: nothing destructive runs unless `\-\-yes` is also given. Also enabled by `IFG_NO_INPUT=1` (`1` or `true`); the flag wins.
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Caller\-chosen key that makes a write safe to repeat after a timeout

The server replays the first response for the same key. Only single\-write commands on routes that support keys accept it (see `ifg schema`, field `accepts_idempotency_key`); any other command exits with code 2 before sending anything. The key is sent as the `Idempotency\-Key` header on that command\*(Aqs write request, and a keyed write is retried with the same key after connection errors, 429 and 5xx. Use a key you chose: ifg never generates one. Allowed characters: A\-Z, a\-z, 0\-9, `.`, `_`, `:`, `\-` (1 to 255). When absent, the environment variable IRONFORGE_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY is used; this flag wins.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbosity: \-v logs each request, \-vv also logs headers
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
